  "id": "larodopa",
  "term": "Larodopa",
  "definition": "Larodopa is another name for levodopa, an amino acid substance that is converted in the brain into dopamine. It is used for Parkinson's disease because it helps make up for reduced dopamine activity in the central nervous system.",
